# ApplicationV2 form controls

## The bug

`<select>`, `<input type="checkbox">`, and `<input type="number">` wired through the ApplicationV2 **`actions` map** + `data-action` fire on **click**, not **change**. Foundry re-renders before the native control finishes → dropdowns snap shut, checkboxes may not toggle.

This recurs on every new UI unless form fields are wired differently from buttons.

## Rules

1. **`actions` map: buttons only** (`<button type="button">`). Never register select/input handlers there.
2. **Form fields: `change` listener in `_onRender`**. Bind once per root element (`dataset.*Bound = "1"`).
3. **Markup**: use `data-field="fieldName"` on selects and inputs. `data-action` on form controls is allowed only when handled **exclusively** in the `change` listener (not in `actions`) — e.g. scavenging `data-action="updateField"`.
4. **Avoid `tag: "form"`** on ApplicationV2 unless native form submit is required.

## Reference implementations

- `src/scavenging/ScavengerLocationApp.ts` — `updateField`, `toggleParty` on `change`
- `src/npcGen/NpcGeneratorApp.ts` — `data-npc-gen-select` on `change`
- `src/hexcrawl/HexcrawlTravelApp.ts` — `data-field` only

## Template

```hbs
{{!-- BAD: handler in actions map --}}
<select data-action="pickToken">...</select>

{{!-- GOOD --}}
<select name="travelTokenId" data-field="travelTokenId">...</select>
```

## Handler sketch

```typescript
protected override async _onRender(context, options) {
  await super._onRender(context, options);
  const root = this.#rootElement();
  if (!root || root.dataset.myAppBound === "1") return;
  root.dataset.myAppBound = "1";
  root.addEventListener("change", (event) => {
    const target = event.target;
    if (!(target instanceof HTMLElement) || !target.dataset.field) return;
    void this.#onFieldChange(target);
  });
}
```
